===Etymology 2===
From the {{etyl|itc-pro|la}} imperative {{m|itc-pro|*kedō|*ke-dō}}, plural {{m|itc-pro|*kedate|*ke-date}}. This is composed of a particle {{m|itc-pro|*ke||here}} (seen also in {{m|la|ecce|ec-ce}}, {{m|la|hic|hi-c}}, {{m|la|illic|illi-c}} etc.) + the imperative of {{m|la|dō||give}} (which was originally {{m|la||*dō}}, but changed later to {{m|la|dā}} by analogy). Equivalent to {{confix|la|ce|do}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{a|Classical}} {{IPA|/ˈke.do/|lang=la}}

====Verb====
''second person singular imperative'' '''cedo''', ''second person plural imperative'' '''{{l|la|cedite}}''' or '''{{l|la|cette}}'''

# {{lb|la|of objects}} Hand (it) over!; Give (it)!
# {{lb|la|with '''{{l|la|manum}}'''}} Give me your hand!
# {{lb|la|of objects|especially evidence or exhibits at a trial}} Produce (it)!; Show (it) to us!
# {{lb|la|of people}} Bring (him)!, Bring (him) in!, Produce (him)!
# Tell me!; Describe (it) to me!, Explain (it) to me!
# {{lb|la|followed by a conditional clause with consequent}} Tell me, Come now, Hear me out
# {{lb|la|followed by a conditional clause without a consequent}} What if?, Suppose?
# {{lb|la|with impersonal or subjunctive}} Come now

